Public WiFi isn’t as safe as it feels
👇👇👇👇👇
1) When you connect to open networks, here’s what can actually happen:
When you connect to open networks, here’s what can actually happen:

Your data can be intercepted
Someone on the same network may see what you’re doing especially on unsecured sites.

Fake WiFi networks (look-alikes)
Hackers can create networks like “Free Airport WiFi” to trick you into connecting.

Session hijacking
They can take over your active logins without needing your password.

Malware injection
Some networks can push harmful files or redirect you to fake websites.

Account theft
If you log into sensitive accounts, your credentials could be captured.
2) How to stay safe:

Avoid logging into banking or email accounts

Don’t enter payment details

Use trusted networks or mobile data

Use VPN. It encrypts your internet traffic so people on the same network can’t easily see what you’re doing.
That means your data is harder to intercept on public WiFi.

Turn off auto-connect to WiFi

Free WiFi is convenient…
but its risky and it can cost you more than you think.
